    {
      "question": "What are employees in Pakhlai?",
      "mode": "auto_fetch",
      "http_status": 200,
      "duration_ms": 8432.781,
      "provider_attempts": 3,
      "answer": {
        "id": 80,
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "In Pakhlai, \"employees\" refers to the staff module: you create staff login and employee records, assign role, shift and kitchen stations, and edit salary profiles (with BranchAdmin restrictions on creating/editing). Around this record, the staff module groups three practical areas:\n\n• Staff accounts (Admin/BranchAdmin): create the employee record with branch, role, status, plus salary basis/base/allowances/deductions/overtime and Payroll Active. Confirm login and station assignment separately from payroll eligibility.\n• Shifts and Attendance (HR → Shifts / Attendance for Admin/BranchAdmin; Shifts / Attendance for OperationsManager): you create or delete shifts and record today's Present / Absent / Leave status for assigned staff, then save. Present is the default; re-saving updates the same shift/date record. Attendance does not automatically calculate payroll hours or deductions, and there is no leave-approval workflow.\n• Salary handoff: employee records feed payroll generation, advance recording, approval and payment — the employee entry is the starting point, not the payment itself.\n\nAn eligible attendance area requires an active branch/restaurant and the appropriate role. Note that I can only describe documented behavior; I have no access to your live staff data.",
        "kind": "answer",
        "state": "complete",
        "error_code": null,
